  "s3": {
    "duration": 26.25,
    "text": "To find it, slide one recording past the other. At each shift, multiply them sample by sample, and add up the products. Mostly, the products are as often negative as positive, and the sum stays small. When the hidden patterns line up, the products turn mostly positive, and the sum jumps. That curve is the cross-correlation. Its peak sits at the delay. x beam computes it this way, through Fourier transforms, on the GPU.",
